en:
"Nooooo!☆"
Imagining the impact to come, I instinctively shut my eyes.
...But no matter how long I waited, the impact never came.{p}

By the time I finally set foot on the first floor, I was drenched in sweat all over.
...I want to hurry up and go home.
The front entrance was just ahead.{p}

......And then.
The door slid open without a sound.
On the other side......{p}

There was another door.
...Huh?
That's strange.{p}

"Well, since you've offered, would you show me the way?"
"Yes, of course.
Shall we go, then...?"{p}

With that, Arai started walking briskly off.
...Where is he going?
Desperate not to lose sight of him, I hurried after Arai.{p}

Well, you see...
It's because you think I'm a dark, gloomy person."
Arai chuckled softly, as if it were terribly funny.{p}

"{a}!"
Arai called my name.
And the next instant...☆{p}

...No.
...I don't want to have this dream.
"Nooooo, I won't!☆"{p}

Over and over... over and over...
A dream that never ends...
A nightmare, and no knowing how long it will go on...{p}

But you see, to me, a date with {b} matters far more than our lives or our tomorrows.
I realized that just a moment ago.
That's why I came back here, even after I'd already made it out.{p}

...I know we don't have time for that, but...
Oh, fine......
I let out a sigh and looked up at Kazama's face.{p}

"Whoa...!"
Suddenly, Kazama lost his balance.
He missed a step...!{p}

"I'm getting out of here, even if I have to go by myself.
Please ask someone else on a date."
I shook off Kazama's arms and stood on the floor of the landing on my own two feet.{p}

But...
Watching him, I started itching to move too.
I think I'll try dancing along with him.{p}

"{b}, take a look at everyone's feet."
Laughing gleefully, Kazama spoke to me.
Everyone's feet...?{p}

There, on my feet, were red shoes all my own...{p}Ahh......
So I have to keep dancing too.
The devil's dance, going on and on with no end in sight......{p}

But to fall down the stairs without a single scratch...
It must be because I'm always such a good girl.
Now, I need to get out of here, fast.{p}

From far off, I could hear police sirens.
Hosoda must have called them.
After seeing this, how many people would ever believe a word I say...?{p}Sinking unsteadily down into the pool of bright red blood, I pictured the red siren lights I would surely be seeing any moment now.{p}
